WEBVTT

00:00:00.351 --> 00:00:16.048
Until now a card carried one label, its priority. Now it also has a category, a sub-category and a complexity. On the card face they sit as small chips right after the priority flag: Frontend, Bug fix, and a complexity of one, drawn as rising bars.

00:00:17.001 --> 00:00:27.880
A label that Obeya suggested and the owner has not touched yet has a purple border. That purple is a magenta, well apart from the violet of a proposal card, and it only ever frames the chip, never the card.

00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:36.821
Unfolded, a card without labels shows four pickers beside each other: priority, category, sub-category and complexity.

00:00:37.775 --> 00:00:50.012
Complexity runs on the steps one, two, three, five and eight. Each step says what it means, in its list and as its tooltip: three is a change across a few files, with tests. A pick takes effect at once.

00:00:50.965 --> 00:01:00.973
Category and sub-category work the same way. Backend, and New feature. Each list ends with None, which takes the label off again and records that the owner chose to leave it empty.

00:01:03.415 --> 00:01:11.426
On a card with suggested labels, any pick makes the label the owner's. Picking the suggested complexity five again keeps the value, and the purple border goes.

00:01:12.448 --> 00:01:24.940
A project has the same pickers on its sheet, and its head shows the chips on a line below the title. That keeps the labels visible while leaving room for the title and the actions. Collapsed, the labels stay above the workstream marks.

00:01:26.884 --> 00:01:35.696
The phone view shows the same chips on its card lists and the same pickers on an unfolded card. A list that would run off the edge of the screen moves left until it fits.

00:01:36.649 --> 00:01:47.295
Every card now carries category, sub-category and complexity beside its priority, set in one click, with Obeya's suggestions marked in purple until the owner takes them over.
